From: handheld-extra
Subject: [PATCH] wlserver: send rerouted volume keys to Steam once, not twice

OGC PR #7 ("reroute synthetic media keys") moved the volume/power key
reroute into wlserver_maybe_reroute_forbidden_key() and reduced the block
in wlserver_handle_key() to a `return`. A later merge of Valve's change to
that same block (the mapPressedHotkeyKeys.erase()) brought the old inline
reroute back underneath the helper call, so a physical volume key now
reaches Steam's surface twice: once from the helper, once from the block.

Steam logs every press as two pairs of OnVolumeButtonPressed and never
changes the volume (AYN Odin 3, 2026-10-21; the Quick Access slider still
works). Keep the erase(), drop the second send.

Still present on the fork's HEAD as of 2026-10-21; drop this patch once
the fork fixes the merge.

---
 src/wlserver.cpp | 19 ++++---------------
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

--- a/src/wlserver.cpp
+++ b/src/wlserver.cpp
@@ -339,21 +339,10 @@
 	if ( ( event->state == WL_KEYBOARD_KEY_STATE_PRESSED || event->state == WL_KEYBOARD_KEY_STATE_RELEASED ) &&
 		 wlserver_maybe_reroute_forbidden_key( keyboard, event->time_msec, event->keycode, event->state ) )
 	{
-		// Always send volume+/- to root server only, to avoid it reaching the game.
-		struct wlr_surface *old_kb_surf = wlserver.kb_focus_surface;
-		struct wlr_surface *new_kb_surf = steamcompmgr_get_server_input_surface( 0 );
-		if ( new_kb_surf )
-		{
-			// This key skips hotkey processing, so drop any press we
-			// recorded for it or the stale sym would wedge every binding.
-			wlserver.mapPressedHotkeyKeys.erase( { keyboard, keycode } );
-
-			wlserver_keyboardfocus( new_kb_surf, false );
-			wlr_seat_set_keyboard( wlserver.wlr.seat, keyboard );
-			wlr_seat_keyboard_notify_key( wlserver.wlr.seat, event->time_msec, event->keycode, event->state );
-			wlserver_keyboardfocus( old_kb_surf, false );
-			return;
-		}
+		// This key skips hotkey processing, so drop any press we
+		// recorded for it or the stale sym would wedge every binding.
+		wlserver.mapPressedHotkeyKeys.erase( { keyboard, keycode } );
+		return;
 	}
 	
 	if ( !wlserver_process_hotkeys( keyboard, event->keycode, event->state == WL_KEYBOARD_KEY_STATE_PRESSED ) )
